#~ " picks the file; a file can be"
#~ " up to FF00 bytes long. **Start** "
#~ "is where it goes, C000 to begin"
#~ " with, and **Length** and **End** "
#~ "show how far it reaches. A file"
#~ " that would run past FFFF is "
#~ "moved down to end there. **OK** "
#~ "writes it into the memory the CPU"
#~ " sees, ROM only with **Allow ROM "
#~ "wr** ticked."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid "**Collect**, and the buttons that reset the counters and export them."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The button with the circular arrows "
#~ "resets all counters, after asking. "
#~ "Loading a snapshot resets them too. "
#~ "The other button saves all counters "
#~ "to a CSV file: one line per "
#~ "byte of RAM and then of ROM, "
#~ "with the columns `type,page,offset,read,write,exec`,"
#~ " untouched bytes included, for a "
#~ "spreadsheet or a script of your "
#~ "own."
#~ msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Open the **Memory Finder** (**Tools >"
#~ " Search**). Many games keep the score"
#~ " as digits: type the digits in "
#~ "**Text** as the game shows them, "
#~ "leading zeros included, such as "
#~ "`000150`. Click **Find**."
#~ msgstr ""

